{"id": "clm:c78df976e60e2e8009cdb8b18d2008fba8d651dc0d81596d9e44892f3ece7241", "type": "statement", "text": "An empty rejectedPlans array is not sufficient evidence that branch candidate trials never happened: SERVER-19350 documents subplanner explain output omitting rejected alternatives, while the r8.0.0 code explicitly runs branch MultiPlanStage selection. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-19350", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "definition", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/r8.0.0/src/mongo/db/exec/subplan.cpp"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:e3ecc7b8a87b8576b24e0d07b94fb8073f1d3131c46683d2c883dddf7f0f357e", "ev:ffdba410b7fbe3f6b33fd4c53c60d1ae19ffeb36d172a003a2723ebf09760415"]}
{"id": "clm:2cec4c8570af9ed66aec8d5b57495c2dd4ab02614b9898a0a2a4db32b2c9f799", "type": "statement", "text": "SORT_MERGE merges ordered index streams. The tagged MongoDB subplanning code separately selects plans for rooted $or branches and contains branch cache machinery. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/sort-results-with-indexes/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "structure", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/r8.0.0/src/mongo/db/exec/subplan.cpp", "https://aws.amazon.com/ko/blogs/tech/documentdb-index-optimization-query-performance/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:dd6678cf8de57921124d7b6db8352d8966d2b56edf6292d8d9194b0b5e3b89a5", "ev:e3ecc7b8a87b8576b24e0d07b94fb8073f1d3131c46683d2c883dddf7f0f357e"]}
{"id": "clm:847494a9795b6457748dd480c7254d7ed764f5ce7fd397ea58ec1fad78e6541b", "type": "statement", "text": "Rooted $or subplanning plans the OR branches independently and combines their index choices into one executable plan; MongoDB 8.0.0's SubplanStage reads active branch cache data and uses MultiPlanStage when branch selection needs trials. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/r8.0.0/src/mongo/db/exec/subplan.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-19350"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:e3ecc7b8a87b8576b24e0d07b94fb8073f1d3131c46683d2c883dddf7f0f357e"]}
{"id": "clm:e19ed2dfebf280177e2340c59f3ac98b6e1e5904132a08ef25845b09754906d2", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB 8.0.0 can fall back from branch subplanning to planning the whole query when subquery planning fails or composite selection returns NoQueryExecutionPlans; the fallback can use a single solution or MultiPlanStage. Other composite-selection errors propagate. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/r8.0.0/src/mongo/db/exec/subplan.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4c507f4a6cdd27fd10690d5343577e3c689dddc94fc1634c2150f705f2d7f275"]}
{"id": "clm:51e48bd152f9cb3f0081a6c05afa6150aac6c3f2b9038077cec4f97ed3fdfd4d", "type": "statement", "text": "The AWS/Miridih case study dated 2026-04-22 reports MongoDB merging indexed type branches with SORT_MERGE for a parent/type/date query, while their DocumentDB deployment sorted the combined results in memory. They split type queries and merged in the application. This is a workload-specific migration observation, not evidence about MongoDB's replanReason. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-04-22)", "source_url": "https://aws.amazon.com/ko/blogs/tech/documentdb-index-optimization-query-performance/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1e4caabd38015a986610c2cefdb36df134b835ce16e829240d756b6f70ab7d60", "ev:8b843a3785a53c52e14cde3c8532c7c336d99e90e004b7c6ea85ee2f7eb55433"]}
{"id": "clm:2739e94ed51fbdc2c5be177b53278fe00dd35641da0b2acc38d16ad462c2cffc", "type": "statement", "text": "Index-supported branch ordering still depends on index design: compound sort directions must match the index pattern or its complete inverse, and sorting on a non-prefix subset requires equality predicates on preceding index keys. SORT_MERGE is not guaranteed merely because every branch has an index. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/sort-results-with-indexes/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-24027"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0a2c3336660a11e371ae9f6bee21ad04b04592bc63acf7e87096dfd55182b24a"]}
{"id": "clm:1fe17ee5b4c1acb0948fc1558377241257bc6dc4f14aa2a90d32a56f1c5f3d47", "type": "statement", "text": "SERVER-91095 describes a historical SBE-subplanning special case: branch entries recovered from the classic cache carry a distinguishing cache-key byte and store neither works nor reads, because rooted-$or replanning was unsupported in that path. Treat this as the issue's implementation context, not a universal statement about every later version. (low confidence) (verified as of 2024-10-15)", "source_url": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-91095", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1513d187824f81ac2135197ecf693691e2a1caefb72368be9fba2467d604ae7f"]}
{"id": "clm:751fb53382992de08466c69c09b00dd37e5a623ab5851bc79b345d88d1a8758e", "type": "statement", "text": "Index direction and collation deserve explicit checks when interpreting SORT_MERGE. SERVER-24027 records an old descending-pagination planning failure, fixed in 3.4.2/3.5.2; SERVER-51120 records a distinct historical collated-key merge correctness bug with patch fixes. Neither ticket establishes a current defect in modern releases. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-24027", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-51120"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:efd392324e3a9f96b221989876b66816be40dacd5921c4256eb5d75b99ac8021", "ev:f6d184500ca7e0b9f005c89a36c61b15e08bb58585042976192f64b2e20f006a"]}
{"id": "clm:b096f49773ff93b8a8bf42d2272ff437ffaf677b94c4f3fa696bd2aa49024c1e", "type": "statement", "text": "In r8.0.0, failed branch planning or failure to obtain a composite solution with NoQueryExecutionPlans can fall back to whole-query planning. Therefore a SUBPLAN wrapper alone does not establish that independent branch planning succeeded. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/r8.0.0/src/mongo/db/exec/subplan.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/r8.0.0/src/mongo/db/exec/subplan.h"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4c507f4a6cdd27fd10690d5343577e3c689dddc94fc1634c2150f705f2d7f275", "ev:c0830391e2b55efef204d4dabbc013025e7f96cb70cd2a779a57b810d442b9e2"]}
{"id": "clm:9e12146bef8361578d56c5e2b00eb9e7cbbb6d8dc8a072b3fdc769dc8ba26b5d", "type": "statement", "text": "The 2018 Database Investigator case contains SUBPLAN with SORT_MERGE over three IXSCAN branches, yet attributes most initial latency to FETCH. An ordered merge plan can therefore coexist with slow document retrieval; stage presence alone does not locate the bottleneck. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://database-investigator.com/2018/10/15/my-first-mongodb-performance-investigation/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:03f10aa2077f58837ea599a00be06f0ad7c68a93f708e7f957af151dceab796a", "ev:bc3b44a5ffa670c936b703decc05c0898d54b78169217d74855c6bc57767eb2c"]}
{"id": "clm:0a77ea9a041f0172bdbd2870acf32ea8bab0162ce2d66d52ae85bf926b511b3f", "type": "statement", "text": "In Phil's 2018 production investigation, an explain execution tree contains SUBPLAN above FETCH, SHARDING_FILTER, and SORT_MERGE, with three IXSCAN children. This is a concrete field example of the stages coexisting, rather than evidence that their presence guarantees a cheap query. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://database-investigator.com/2018/10/15/my-first-mongodb-performance-investigation/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:03f10aa2077f58837ea599a00be06f0ad7c68a93f708e7f957af151dceab796a", "ev:bc3b44a5ffa670c936b703decc05c0898d54b78169217d74855c6bc57767eb2c"]}
{"id": "clm:33001b53e84a16165b9fed368c8dfd7981b3e08ed540a8624910312a156804b4", "type": "statement", "text": "In r8.0.0, canUseSubplanning rejects queries with hint, min, max, or a tailable cursor; it requires a nonempty OR at the canonical expression root. Merely containing a nested $or does not satisfy that test. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/r8.0.0/src/mongo/db/exec/subplan.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5c488e9cd25fda6564da86209abb78e41334f8df8bca21c3d096a7a1c65bb28b"]}
{"id": "clm:881101fc49a6c6a8c32a8e26592a1f2ff4a6399d860734f8ff182a372b958f9e", "type": "statement", "text": "SORT_MERGE merges already ordered index-scan streams to provide the requested sort order. It does not mean a blocking SORT occurred. An indexed $or can use separate indexes per clause to support one sort, provided the selected inputs supply compatible ordering. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/sort-results-with-indexes/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://dev.to/mongodb/or-expansion-in-mongodb-and-how-in-is-treated-as-a-range-with-skip-scan-or-an-equality-for-2b38", "https://aws.amazon.com/ko/blogs/tech/documentdb-index-optimization-query-performance/", "https://database-investigator.com/2018/10/15/my-first-mongodb-performance-investigation/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:22ced08a3612f390a50aa992f517754be26d366dcd67b43a2cbd1a9ff4a3bb93", "ev:36a6fd39e0e6c7d0e82de744553a80a4e5cf2f98b923baca978f76200783157b"]}
{"id": "clm:2b758fa7cc8179b71e8e70d03760a09aa037a032cca10311149a4dd05379a2db", "type": "statement", "text": "SORT_MERGE alone does not establish that rooted-OR branch subplanning occurred: the documented engineering example also obtains SORT_MERGE from a small $in list by exploding equality intervals into ordered IXSCANs. Inspect the surrounding plan and canonical predicate. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://dev.to/mongodb/or-expansion-in-mongodb-and-how-in-is-treated-as-a-range-with-skip-scan-or-an-equality-for-2b38", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/r8.0.0/src/mongo/db/exec/subplan.cpp"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0b41c9f65607c6ec13d5f137399b969242813ef2e80542bf9024210eb7f86f93", "ev:5c488e9cd25fda6564da86209abb78e41334f8df8bca21c3d096a7a1c65bb28b"]}
{"id": "clm:2c8b3c069fa243d6dd682f760641cb085996581594f0ea45a90cdad6727d2538", "type": "statement", "text": "SERVER-18777 documents a branch-cache exception: SubplanStage can reuse an $or branch without CachedPlanStage's trial, allowing a poor branch plan to persist without the usual eviction and replanning. SERVER-91095's 2024 description likewise says SBE subplanning branch entries carry neither works nor reads. These records describe that path, not every execution of every OR-shaped query. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2024-10-15)", "source_url": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-18777", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-91095"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1513d187824f81ac2135197ecf693691e2a1caefb72368be9fba2467d604ae7f", "ev:82380c64db2414601cecbbaa291b9eaf70f293ebbdbc753e62111173a0b44964"]}
{"id": "clm:a274219acfdbb34f196d3998320c378bfa6804d988e226237a9194064b435a4f", "type": "statement", "text": "Replanning and choosing a subplanner are separate decisions. SERVER-120492 describes restarting planning while explicitly excluding subplanning; SERVER-121973 reports a regression where that exclusion was lost and tassert 8746609 fired after data growth. The latter ticket lists fixes in 8.3.0-rc2 and 9.0.0-rc0. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-09-20)", "source_url": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-120492", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-121973"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6f96b12108f19f472e7206121817557b542c43d2a2938f8633a9a17f2b83ea85", "ev:a2af33746a936ec7b2e4a20976f09d6f53929b4af18522f7bc407293d0aed974"]}
{"id": "clm:9727092716f1203f7ecd394f58b70202248cb0dbfce8f602458bb029aedd1f33", "type": "statement", "text": "A forum user's statement that $or always uses SORT_MERGE should not be generalized. MongoDB's index-sort documentation makes ordered index support conditional, and the historical scan-direction bug demonstrates that an OR plan can instead require a blocking sort. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/community/forums/t/when-in-can-use-sort-merge/201141", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/sort-results-with-indexes/", "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-24027"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:36a6fd39e0e6c7d0e82de744553a80a4e5cf2f98b923baca978f76200783157b", "ev:52bcc53d7a16cb63088a71094068aae743b94d2a7633a3a019df62c2848cb25f", "ev:f6d184500ca7e0b9f005c89a36c61b15e08bb58585042976192f64b2e20f006a"]}
{"id": "clm:cadf4ca2ba18c56ab9f988a4b3cbfaa076a1a8bb1b253d1d95778363523c085e", "type": "statement", "text": "In MongoDB r8.0.0, SubplanStage plans the clauses of a rooted $or independently, ranks branch candidates with MultiPlanStage, and builds a composite solution from the winning branches. Rooted refers to the canonical match-expression root being OR. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/r8.0.0/src/mongo/db/exec/subplan.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/r8.0.0/src/mongo/db/exec/subplan.h"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4c507f4a6cdd27fd10690d5343577e3c689dddc94fc1634c2150f705f2d7f275", "ev:c0830391e2b55efef204d4dabbc013025e7f96cb70cd2a779a57b810d442b9e2"]}
{"id": "clm:400fcf2f2ebef9be6f5cee41a2f1c0c5b7a1a33642098235d3bbbb686ab67907", "type": "statement", "text": "The r8.0.0 SubplanStage caching strategy operates per clause: it can recover branch index tags from an active classic-cache entry and reuse branch shapes across queries. Its documented successful-subplanning strategy does not read or write a cached composite rooted-$or plan. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/r8.0.0/src/mongo/db/exec/subplan.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/r8.0.0/src/mongo/db/exec/subplan.h"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:c0830391e2b55efef204d4dabbc013025e7f96cb70cd2a779a57b810d442b9e2", "ev:e3ecc7b8a87b8576b24e0d07b94fb8073f1d3131c46683d2c883dddf7f0f357e"]}
{"id": "clm:04c0fcdc873867622a3f3000f4983d6870a73d42a522d37cdb721fe75387f0a3", "type": "statement", "text": "SERVER-121973 records tassert 8746609 after a cached rooted-$or query replans following document growth: the replanning path unexpectedly created a SubPlanner. The issue lists fixes in 8.3.0-rc2 and 9.0.0-rc0. This is a specific regression, not proof that every rooted-$or query replans. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-09-20)", "source_url": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-121973", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Rooted $or subplanning and SORT_MERGE"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:0790df979300c7ef43b736e97f36c0e4017847f9438d8ff61bfe3f964c43ef8b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a2af33746a936ec7b2e4a20976f09d6f53929b4af18522f7bc407293d0aed974"]}
